# item30: Plage01 route, walked end to end. No teleport commands. Segments A-D are the measured
# walks from local/reports/item30-plage01-walk.md (hut, beach nav walk incl. the running jump
# over the crate wall, TouchTrigger7 + killer, truck return legs + Porte1).
#
# The `weapon XIII.m60` grant stays (t=51.30, the game's own `Weapon.GiveTo`/`ChangedWeapon`
# path). NOTE (item30c round 8, measured): with the item61 anti-tamper gate the beach soldiers
# are at their authored strength (150 hp) and ACTIVE from their landing, so the walk fights the
# soldiers it meets instead of tanking them. Measured damage sources (r8 probe runs, report
# round 8): `BaseSoldier` stands 9 UU off the hut exit (fires from ~72 s); `BaseSoldier7`
# charges into the crate-wall crossing (~3.6 hp/s there; both first round-8 walk runs died at
# ~200 s exactly there); `BaseSoldier4` hunts along the shore to the crates and fires on the
# crossing; `BaseSoldier8` (the heli magnum sniper) walks to the (-5902,-10424) legs and dealt
# ~45 hp there. Each is killed with the granted m60 (contact 45/hit) at its measured arrival,
# fitted inside the schedule's existing wait windows. Truck-shore soldiers BaseSoldier9/10
# are killed before the killer fight below.
#
# Round 8 uses the truck-shore stand after T7 rather than the old T8 scene and distant chase.
# The killer hunts the player's shore position and settles at the water's edge. The route
# fights him there, walks onto his corpse for the game's own auto-search, then follows the
# return legs to Porte1. switch_weapon 2 requests the picked-up Beretta before the killer fight.
#
# The killer (BaseSoldier6) walks while attacking, so the view is tracked onto it around the
# firing (`track BaseSoldier6` / `track off`).
#
# item76 (measured, scratch local/re/item76): `Pawn.PressingFire` now reads the controller's
# `bFire` byte, so automatic AI weapons fire real bursts (the hut-exit `BaseSoldier`'s kalash
# took 147 -> 93 hp in 4 s under the old schedule; the old route died at 158 s). Re-timed by
# input only: the hut-exit soldier is shot as he wakes (head aim, he dies at 72.9 s),
# BaseSoldier4 is killed from the (-877,-8153) wait stand where he otherwise fires for 8 s, the
# crate-wall stand clears its unreached goto so the tracked aim is not overridden, and the
# killer is approached to ~250 UU before the Beretta burst. A `goto` that never comes within
# 24 UU stays active and keeps driving the yaw, so a stand that fires is entered with a `goto`
# to the spot the player actually stops on.

# ---- hut: key, Beretta, door (all walked) ------------------------------------------------
# All times include the +2.2 s intro offset measured after the origin/main merge (control
# returns at ~46.8 s now, not ~45.0 s): inputs issued while the intro suppresses input are
# dropped, so the segment A jumps must land after the handback.
t=51.30 weapon XIII.m60
t=47.20 goto -491.84 -314.14
t=47.60 jump
t=48.10 jump
t=48.60 jump
t=49.10 jump
t=49.60 jump
t=50.10 forward 0
t=51.20 goto -560.0 -520.0
t=53.70 yaw 180
t=53.80 forward 1
t=53.90 jump
t=54.40 forward 0
t=55.20 goto -700.0 -511.89
t=57.20 forward 0
t=58.20 goto -500.0 -620.0
t=61.70 goto -521.9 -724.9
t=65.70 yaw 314.891
t=65.80 forward 1
t=67.30 forward 0
t=67.40 goto -250.0 -1226.0
t=70.40 yaw 268.0
t=70.50 use
t=71.00 use
t=71.50 use
t=71.80 forward 1
# Hut-exit soldier kill (item76, measured): BaseSoldier stands at (-299,-1408) and wakes as the
# player touches TouchTrigger9 at ~72.0 s; his kalash bursts from 72.25 s. The player stops on
# the hut steps and fires at his head straight away: he dies at 72.9 s (r5: 147 -> 141 hp here,
# against 147 -> 93 hp when the old schedule fired from 74.7 s, run c_orig).
t=72.30 forward 0
t=72.30 engage BaseSoldier 1500 10
# TouchTrigger9 (-307,-1396) on the way down; objective 0 completes in the game's own chain.
t=73.50 goto -307.0 -1400.0

# ---- beach: nav polyline southwest to the truck shore ------------------------------------
# Waypoints are the map's decoded ReachSpec polyline. The distance/150 + 2 s per goto is a
# lead-time SCHEDULE, not a speed claim: the player walks at the sim's decoded GroundSpeed
# 472 UU/s (measured max sample 472.2 in the route run; AccelRate 2048 reaches it in 0.23 s),
# median 352.6 UU/s while moving over the shore legs (per-leg re-acceleration and cornering),
# and 150 UU/s is 2.3x below that, so the waypoint is always reached before the next command
# fires (the route then stands at the waypoint: 66% of the shore window is scheduled waiting,
# longest spans 5.5-7 s match the schedule gaps). The margin exists because earlier walked
# segments measured per-leg stalls (ramps, corners, the crate-wall notch) at 143-180 UU/s
# leg pace; the schedule keeps the route robust to them. The crate
# wall at the west end (stack top 1132 vs the 1067 passerelle shelf) is crossed with a running
# jump - UE2 movement: 65 UU is above the 35 UU step and below the 92.8 UU jump apex.
t=77.70 goto 643.3 -2397.5
t=82.30 goto 495.7 -2753.6
t=88.20 goto -6.5 -3041.7
t=94.90 goto 256.4 -3696.2
t=101.70 goto 527.7 -4360.9
t=107.00 goto 422.3 -4846.9
t=114.50 goto -78.5 -5502.2
t=124.10 goto 98.1 -6628.7
t=133.80 goto -909.8 -7179.3
t=141.30 goto -805.2 -7997.7
t=144.20 goto -861.8 -8127.4
# BaseSoldier4 kill (item76, measured): he follows the shore to 200-600 UU of this wait stand
# and keeps firing (control run without this block: he hits the player 26 times from 132 to
# 194 s, 127 -> 106 hp over this wait alone, and the player dies at 299 s). The player stops
# on the spot he reaches, (-877,-8153) (the goto above ends 30 UU short, so it stays active and
# would keep the yaw), and bursts him: he dies at 147.1 s (r5).
t=146.40 goto -877.1 -8153.1
t=146.50 engage BaseSoldier4 2000 10
t=152.90 goto -1686.3 -8702.9
t=160.90 goto -2554.9 -8907.9
t=169.10 goto -3413.6 -9257.6
t=172.90 goto -3665.9 -9354.3
t=177.30 goto -3990.0 -9424.0
t=181.60 goto -4119.0 -9427.7
t=182.10 jump
t=182.90 jump
t=183.70 jump
t=184.50 jump
t=185.30 jump
t=186.10 jump
t=189.70 goto -4319.9 -9475.7
# Crate-wall ambush kill (round 8, measured): BaseSoldier7 charges into the crossing (his fire
# measured ~3.6 hp/s; both first round-8 walk runs died at ~200 s exactly here) - the player
# stands at (-4319,-9475) in the schedule's wait window and bursts him with the m60 (contact
# 45/hit). item76: the goto above stops 34 UU short at (-4347.7,-9495.1) and would keep the
# yaw, so it is replaced by the reached spot before the tracked burst (measured r5:
# BaseSoldier7 dies at 190.8 s on the first two hits).
t=190.10 goto -4347.7 -9495.1
t=190.20 engage BaseSoldier7 2000 10
# BaseSoldier4 hunted along the shore from the east and parks 300-600 UU north-east of the
# crossing; burst him from the same stand - before walking past BaseSoldier7's corpse, which
# sits directly on the firing line afterwards (measured: the post-leg burst hit the corpse).
t=192.10 engage BaseSoldier4 2000 10
t=195.30 goto -4630.0 -9531.7
t=202.70 goto -5568.0 -9793.0
t=209.50 goto -5902.0 -10424.5
# BS8 kill (round 8, measured): the heli magnum sniper drops at (-6139,-13860) at ~193 s,
# walks the shore and hovers around (-5902,-10424) - 150-250 UU off this leg. Walking past him
# unharmed measured ~45 hp of magnum fire (the first round-8 route run), so the player bursts
# him here at contact range.
t=210.60 engage BaseSoldier8 2000 10
t=213.20 goto -5839.7 -10664.2
t=217.80 goto -5738.4 -11048.0
t=223.20 goto -5445.3 -11461.0
t=228.50 goto -5103.0 -11821.9
t=234.50 goto -4557.0 -12080.8
t=240.60 goto -4011.9 -12352.8
t=244.50 goto -3731.0 -12423.8
t=247.40 goto -3602.6 -12453.4
t=254.00 goto -2941.9 -12662.5
t=263.40 goto -2029.2 -13286.1
t=271.20 goto -1191.2 -13523.4
t=278.90 goto -366.7 -13757.3
t=288.20 goto 643.2 -14174.5


# fight-probe cut: the opt-in fight tests (plage01_killer_awake_prefix) take the route only up
# to this line. The T7 shore touch above (~289.6 s) has woken BaseSoldier6 out of his
# IAController `faction` stasis; he then hunts the player's position and stops at the water's
# edge ~730 UU short of the truck shore (measured round 8, scratch r8_e1/r8_e2). Everything
# after this line is the truck-shore stand-and-fight, the corpse search and the truck ending.

# ---- truck-shore stand: BaseSoldier9 (-163,-13066, 110 hp) holds LOS on the whole parking and
# shore area; BaseSoldier10 (patrolling (470,-16267)..(-154,-15758), 150 hp) reaches the shore
# too. Both must die before anything else or they pin the player wherever he stands (measured
# round 8: -12/10 s each). The hut-granted m60 (switch_weapon 16, its decoded InventoryGroup)
# reaches them with `track` aim at 1540/2750 UU, 45 hp/hit, every fired round landing (measured
# r8_e2). The fires start as the player arrives at PathNode47 (the goto above lands ~291).
t=291.10 switch_weapon 16
t=291.30 engage BaseSoldier9 3500 20
t=291.40 engage BaseSoldier10 3500 20
# ---- the killer: he settles at the water's edge ~(1100,-13750) from ~300 s (r8_e2) and stays
# there while the player holds the shore. switch_weapon 2 requests the picked-up Beretta
# (InventoryGroup 2) before the burst; the checkpoint acceptance also checks its selection
# after the corpse search. The firing window below is measured to kill his authored 125 hp.
# item76 (measured r5): from the 630 UU stand no round reached him (0 hits in 15), and a fire
# during the M60's 0.67 s DownWeapon aborted the switch. The player now walks to ~250 UU of him
# while the Beretta comes up, then fires head-aimed from 304.4 s: he dies at 305.0 s.
t=302.60 switch_weapon 2
t=303.00 goto_until 947.0 -13924.0 arrived 10
t=303.10 engage BaseSoldier6 3000 20
# ---- corpse walk: the game's own XIIIPlayerPawn.Tick auto-search drains the killer's chain
# (the truck key) as the player walks over him (measured r8_e2: Touch BaseSoldier6 at ~309,
# then `use Porte1: Unlocked`). item76 (measured): the killer now dies coming at the player and
# his corpse comes to rest at (1391.6,-13495.1) (diagnostic run to 311 s), so the walk aims
# there instead of the old (1170,-13700) hover spot.
t=311.50 loot 2500 20
# Measured: the pre-save run left the M60 selected. Re-select the Beretta through the game's
# normal switch after the auto-search, preserving the checkpoint's expected selection.
t=315.00 switch_weapon 2
# ---- return along the measured back-route legs (r8_e2 walked these exact lines): Porte2
# opens on approach, the T8 detour is unnecessary with the killer dead (measured: the travel
# chain is the key + Porte1 only). The shore squad was killed before the killer fight.
t=318.00 goto 1227.0 -12624.0
t=325.00 goto 1294.0 -12566.0
t=327.00 goto 1282.0 -13568.0
t=334.00 goto 643.0 -14174.0
t=341.00 goto 1215.0 -14000.0
# ---- truck ending: Porte1 (the pick-up truck's door) unlocks through the corpse-searched key
# and triggers the level-end cinematic; PlayerTick then turns it into the ServerTravel to
# banque01 (the final fixture uses Porte1 at t=345-346; measure travel in the route test).
t=345.00 yaw 270.0
t=345.10 use Porte1
t=346.10 use Porte1
t=347.00 wait_travel
